1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,964
October 2026.

2
00:00:00,964 --> 00:00:05,563
After three decades, Street
Fighter is back on the big screen.

3
00:00:05,563 --> 00:00:11,645
And in its final act, a demon walks down
off a mountain, steps into the arena, and

4
00:00:11,645 --> 00:00:15,947
finishes the tournament's
champion in a matter of seconds.

5
00:00:15,947 --> 00:00:20,471
If you haven't seen the movie
yet, this is your last warning.

6
00:00:20,471 --> 00:00:23,586
Because today, we are spoiling everything.

7
00:00:24,786 --> 00:00:27,143
Welcome back to Don't Spoil It RG.

8
00:00:27,143 --> 00:00:32,688
This is Street Fighter, directed by Kitao
Sakurai, from Legendary and Paramount.

9
00:00:32,688 --> 00:00:38,372
We're breaking down the beginning, every
major fight, the plot twists, the ending,

10
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:39,897
and the credits scene.

11
00:00:39,897 --> 00:00:45,580
And we're keeping two things separate: what
actually happens on screen, and what's

12
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:47,729
only fan theory about a sequel.

13
00:00:47,729 --> 00:00:52,096
Whenever we cross into theory,
you'll see it flagged on screen.

14
00:00:53,297 --> 00:00:54,660
Quick roster check.

15
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:56,023
Andrew Koji is Ryu.

16
00:00:56,023 --> 00:00:57,529
Noah Centineo is Ken.

17
00:00:57,529 --> 00:00:59,322
Callina Liang is Chun-Li.

18
00:00:59,322 --> 00:01:01,043
David Dastmalchian is M.

19
00:01:01,043 --> 00:01:05,203
Bison, and Roman Reigns, credited
as Joe Anoa'i, is Akuma.

20
00:01:05,203 --> 00:01:11,228
Jason Momoa plays Blanka, Cody Rhodes is
Guile, 50 Cent is Balrog, Vidyut Jammwal is

21
00:01:11,228 --> 00:01:13,667
Dhalsim, and Orville Peck is Vega.

22
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:19,692
Quick note: our animated versions are drawn
from the classic arcade designs, not the

23
00:01:19,692 --> 00:01:20,194
actors.

24
00:01:21,393 --> 00:01:27,427
The story opens in 1987, in Thailand, at
the very first World Warrior Tournament.

25
00:01:27,427 --> 00:01:33,685
A young Ryu fights his way to the final
against the giant Muay Thai king, Sagat, and

26
00:01:33,685 --> 00:01:34,058
wins.

27
00:01:34,058 --> 00:01:35,250
But not cleanly.

28
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:41,359
To win, Ryu lets something dark into his
fighting, and the film treats those inner

29
00:01:41,359 --> 00:01:43,221
demons as literally real.

30
00:01:43,221 --> 00:01:49,181
That surge of killing intent reaches
someone who has been waiting for it: Akuma.

31
00:01:49,181 --> 00:01:53,577
In the aftermath, Ryu's master,
Gouken, is killed by Akuma.

32
00:01:53,577 --> 00:01:56,184
And Ryu walks away from everything.

33
00:01:56,184 --> 00:01:56,929
His title.

34
00:01:56,929 --> 00:01:57,898
His training.

35
00:01:57,898 --> 00:01:59,462
His best friend, Ken.

36
00:02:00,662 --> 00:02:04,673
Six years later, in 1993,
the two have drifted apart.

37
00:02:04,673 --> 00:02:10,047
Ryu is living in self-imposed exile,
wandering, barely fighting at all.

38
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:12,393
Ken Masters went the other way.

39
00:02:12,393 --> 00:02:18,144
He's a showman now, a fighter for the
cameras, all flash and no real stakes.

40
00:02:18,144 --> 00:02:19,809
Then Chun-Li shows up.

41
00:02:19,809 --> 00:02:25,334
She needs both of them inside a
brand-new event: the second World Warrior

42
00:02:25,334 --> 00:02:26,167
Tournament.

43
00:02:26,167 --> 00:02:32,146
And the old wound between Ryu and Ken
tears open the second they're in the same

44
00:02:32,146 --> 00:02:32,524
room.

45
00:02:33,724 --> 00:02:35,827
Here's the first big reveal.

46
00:02:35,827 --> 00:02:38,004
Chun-Li isn't just a fighter.

47
00:02:38,004 --> 00:02:43,261
She's an undercover Interpol agent,
and this isn't just a job for her.

48
00:02:43,261 --> 00:02:44,313
It's personal.

49
00:02:44,313 --> 00:02:44,463
M.

50
00:02:44,463 --> 00:02:46,265
Bison killed her father.

51
00:02:46,265 --> 00:02:52,498
She's been working her way toward him for
years, and this tournament is the closest

52
00:02:52,498 --> 00:02:54,000
she has ever gotten.

53
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:57,688
Because the tournament is a front.

54
00:02:57,688 --> 00:03:03,760
Bison, played by David Dastmalchian, is
running a scheme for global domination, and

55
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,443
what he wants is power.

56
00:03:05,443 --> 00:03:08,882
More Psycho Power than
any human has ever held.

57
00:03:08,882 --> 00:03:14,955
His operation drains Hado energy from
fighters, so gathering the strongest warriors

58
00:03:14,955 --> 00:03:19,783
on the planet in one place is
basically building himself a buffet.

59
00:03:19,783 --> 00:03:22,710
But the fighters are only the appetizer.

60
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:27,466
The real target is the most
dangerous dark power on Earth: Akuma.

61
00:03:27,466 --> 00:03:32,441
And the one person who can draw
Akuma down from his mountain is Ryu.

62
00:03:33,641 --> 00:03:38,777
Before a single official match, the
fighters collide in a nightclub.

63
00:03:38,777 --> 00:03:44,820
Ken, Ryu, Guile, Dhalsim, Vega and Balrog
all end up in one glorious, ridiculous

64
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:45,273
brawl.

65
00:03:45,273 --> 00:03:51,315
It's the movie at its most fun, and Cody
Rhodes' Guile gets some of the funniest

66
00:03:51,315 --> 00:03:52,675
lines in the film.

67
00:03:53,876 --> 00:03:56,414
Then comes the tournament proper.

68
00:03:56,414 --> 00:04:02,412
Honestly, it gets less screen time than
a lot of fans hoped, only a handful of

69
00:04:02,412 --> 00:04:02,873
bouts.

70
00:04:02,873 --> 00:04:04,796
But Ken makes them count.

71
00:04:04,796 --> 00:04:08,641
He takes down Balrog, 50
Cent's heavyweight boxer.

72
00:04:08,641 --> 00:04:10,333
Then he beats Dhalsim.

73
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:16,331
Suddenly the showman is one win away from
the title, and for the first time in

74
00:04:16,331 --> 00:04:19,945
years, he's fighting like
he actually means it.

75
00:04:21,145 --> 00:04:24,331
Ryu, meanwhile, never
makes it to his match.

76
00:04:24,331 --> 00:04:25,707
Bison captures him.

77
00:04:25,707 --> 00:04:31,500
And to force Ryu's power to the surface,
Bison makes him fight Blanka, played by

78
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:37,510
Jason Momoa, feral and crackling with
electricity, while he watches the dark energy

79
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:38,524
start to rise.

80
00:04:39,724 --> 00:04:42,084
Now the movie's emotional twist.

81
00:04:42,084 --> 00:04:46,731
The reason Ryu and Ken fell apart
wasn't just Ryu disappearing.

82
00:04:46,731 --> 00:04:52,779
Ryu finally confesses that back in 1987,
jealousy drove him to sabotage Ken's shot

83
00:04:52,779 --> 00:04:54,623
at that first tournament.

84
00:04:54,623 --> 00:04:57,942
That's the secret he's
carried for six years.

85
00:04:57,942 --> 00:05:01,778
And in the fight that follows,
Ryu beats Ken anyway.

86
00:05:01,778 --> 00:05:04,138
Ken never makes it to the final.

87
00:05:05,338 --> 00:05:08,586
Which leads to the
cruelest beat in the film.

88
00:05:08,586 --> 00:05:14,505
Promoter Don Sauvage, played by Eric André,
is thrilled that Ken is a no-show, and

89
00:05:14,505 --> 00:05:19,991
he declares Joe, played by UFC champion
Alexander Volkanovski, the winner by

90
00:05:19,991 --> 00:05:20,569
forfeit.

91
00:05:20,569 --> 00:05:25,694
Joe only got this far because Ryu,
his original opponent, was captured.

92
00:05:25,694 --> 00:05:31,036
And then Akuma descends from his mountain
and challenges the new champion.

93
00:05:31,036 --> 00:05:32,985
Seconds later, Joe is down.

94
00:05:32,985 --> 00:05:34,717
And it seems, he's dead.

95
00:05:35,917 --> 00:05:39,055
Ryu arrives and challenges Akuma alone.

96
00:05:39,055 --> 00:05:40,905
And he can't win clean.

97
00:05:40,905 --> 00:05:45,250
So he does the one thing he
swore he'd never do again.

98
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:47,020
He lets the hatred in.

99
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:52,170
This is Evil Ryu, the version
longtime fans know from the games.

100
00:05:52,170 --> 00:05:53,859
Evil Ryu beats Akuma.

101
00:05:53,859 --> 00:05:56,756
But the darkness doesn't switch off.

102
00:05:56,756 --> 00:05:59,089
Ryu turns on his own friends.

103
00:06:00,290 --> 00:06:04,975
Then comes the payoff the whole
movie has been building to.

104
00:06:04,975 --> 00:06:11,567
Ken, the one who never could, plants his
feet, cups his hands, and finally throws a

105
00:06:11,567 --> 00:06:12,679
real Hadouken.

106
00:06:12,679 --> 00:06:16,014
It hits Ryu and snaps him back to himself.

107
00:06:17,214 --> 00:06:22,616
But while the heroes were fighting each
other, Bison collected the real prize.

108
00:06:22,616 --> 00:06:26,563
His men restrain the unconscious
Akuma and haul him away.

109
00:06:26,563 --> 00:06:32,035
Ryu, Ken, Chun-Li and Dan chase after
them, until Cammy destroys their vehicle.

110
00:06:32,035 --> 00:06:33,004
Bison escapes.

111
00:06:33,004 --> 00:06:33,766
With Akuma.

112
00:06:34,966 --> 00:06:37,417
So here's where the movie lands.

113
00:06:37,417 --> 00:06:42,626
Bison is free, and the most dangerous
fighter alive is his prisoner.

114
00:06:42,626 --> 00:06:44,005
Akuma is not dead.

115
00:06:44,005 --> 00:06:50,286
And notice what the film doesn't show: we
never actually see Bison extract Akuma's

116
00:06:50,286 --> 00:06:50,745
power.

117
00:06:50,745 --> 00:06:52,967
That's being saved for later.

118
00:06:52,967 --> 00:06:59,248
Meanwhile, Guile and Dhalsim pick up our
heroes, and Ryu, Ken, Chun-Li and Dan hit

119
00:06:59,248 --> 00:07:02,082
the road together to hunt Bison down.

120
00:07:02,082 --> 00:07:05,299
A lot of viewers found that ending abrupt.

121
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:10,968
The movie builds Bison up as the big
bad, then spends its climax on Akuma.

122
00:07:10,968 --> 00:07:15,104
But it's clearly designed to
leave the door wide open.

123
00:07:16,303 --> 00:07:20,974
And stay in your seat, because
there's an animated credits scene.

124
00:07:20,974 --> 00:07:27,011
Some outlets call it mid-credits, others
post-credits, so watch all the way through.

125
00:07:27,011 --> 00:07:32,544
Somewhere tropical, Bison and his
lieutenants approach a towering man with an

126
00:07:32,544 --> 00:07:35,562
eyepatch and a huge scar across his chest.

127
00:07:35,562 --> 00:07:38,868
It's Sagat, the man Ryu
defeated back in 1987.

128
00:07:38,868 --> 00:07:41,958
And Bison is here to
offer him an alliance.

129
00:07:43,159 --> 00:07:45,474
Let's lock in what's confirmed.

130
00:07:45,474 --> 00:07:48,910
Chun-Li is Interpol, out
to avenge her father.

131
00:07:48,910 --> 00:07:51,226
Ryu sabotaged Ken back in 1987.

132
00:07:51,226 --> 00:07:54,512
Akuma killed Gouken,
and Joe appears to die.

133
00:07:54,512 --> 00:07:58,919
Ryu became Evil Ryu and came
back thanks to Ken's Hadouken.

134
00:07:58,919 --> 00:08:01,235
Bison escaped with Akuma alive.

135
00:08:01,235 --> 00:08:03,849
And Sagat is now in Bison's sights.

136
00:08:05,048 --> 00:08:06,271
Now, theory time.

137
00:08:06,271 --> 00:08:12,241
None of this is confirmed, and no sequel
had been officially announced when we made

138
00:08:12,241 --> 00:08:13,032
this video.

139
00:08:13,032 --> 00:08:18,067
Theory one: Bison drains Akuma and
becomes something far beyond human.

140
00:08:18,067 --> 00:08:23,821
Theory two: Sagat joins Bison out of
revenge, setting up Ryu versus Sagat, round

141
00:08:23,821 --> 00:08:24,108
two.

142
00:08:24,108 --> 00:08:28,496
Theory three: Ryu's dark side
isn't gone, it's just sleeping.

143
00:08:28,496 --> 00:08:34,034
Theory four: Gouken could come back,
because in the games, he survived Akuma.

144
00:08:34,034 --> 00:08:36,552
And theory five: Cammy, Zangief, E.

145
00:08:36,552 --> 00:08:40,220
Honda and the rest finally
get real arcs next time.

146
00:08:41,421 --> 00:08:43,271
So what did you think?

147
00:08:43,271 --> 00:08:46,887
Did the ending land,
or did it feel rushed?

148
00:08:46,887 --> 00:08:53,782
Tell me in the comments, hit subscribe,
and remember: on this channel, we spoil it

149
00:08:53,782 --> 00:08:55,547
so you don't have to.

150
00:08:55,547 --> 00:08:57,145
See you next round.
